  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes to `ranges.mjs`\n\nI rewrote `mergeRanges(ranges)` to meet all requirements:\n\n**Validation (throws `TypeError`):**\n- Input must be an array.\n- Each element must be a pair array of length 2.\n- Both bounds must be safe integers (`Number.isSafeInteger`).\n- `start <= end` must hold.\n\n**Merging logic:**\n- **No mutation:** The input array and its pairs are never touched. I build a fresh `sorted` array via `.map(([start, end]) => [start, end])` before sorting, so the original pairs are copied.\n- **Sort by start, then end:** `sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1])`.\n- **Overlap or adjacency:** The condition `range[0] <= last[1] + 1` merges intervals that overlap *or* touch as adjacent integers (e.g. `[2,4]` + `[5,7]` → `[2,7]`).\n- **Contained intervals don't shorten:** The merge only extends when `range[1] > last[1]`, so a contained interval like `[3,4]` inside `[1,10]` leaves the end at `10`.\n- **Fresh output:** The result array and every pair in it are newly created arrays.\n- **Empty input:** Returns `[]`.\n\n**Verification against the provided tests:**\n- `mergeRanges([[8,10],[1,3],[2,5]])` → `[[1,5],[8,10]]` ✓\n- `mergeRanges([[5,7],[2,4]])` → `[[2,7]]` ✓\n\nThe named export `mergeRanges` is preserved.",
